                        "tree_id":  "895763945adaffa7e600198fd18a611870064d5c",
                        "message":  "fix(dast): make the authenticated ZAP scan resilient + valid OpenAPI 3.1 doc\n\nThe first authenticated DAST run aborted in the openapi job: one endpoint read\ntimed out and the parser rejected the definition, so with failOnError the plan\nstopped before spider/activeScan and produced no report at all.\n\n- .zap/zap-jwt-config.yaml\n  - failOnError: false + continueOnFailure: true so a single flaky endpoint\n    cannot abort the scan; the pipeline gate stays the authority\n  - passiveScan-config: scanOnlyInContext -\u003e scanOnlyInScope (correct param)\n  - passiveScan-wait: maxDuration 5 -\u003e 1 (the param is in minutes)\n  - new export job writing the reached URL list (scanned_urls.txt) as evidence\n- pipeline-4-dast-scan.yml\n  - gate now also fails when the scan reached fewer than 10 URLs, so a run that\n    silently authenticated nothing cannot look like a clean scan\n- OpenApiConfig: add info.license.identifier, which OpenAPI 3.1 requires next\n  to info.license.name (strict parsers such as ZAP rejected the whole doc)",
                        "timestamp":  "2026-10-21T15:23:46Z",
                        "author":  {
                                       "name":  "luannv",
                                       "email":  "vanluan.dev@gmail.com"
                                   },
                        "committer":  {
                                          "name":  "luannv",
                                          "email":  "vanluan.dev@gmail.com"
                                      }
                    },
